# Deep Context Code Review Report
## TradeQuip Platform (TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY)

**Date**: January 28, 2026  
**Scope**: Full codebase architecture, security, and code quality analysis

---

## Executive Summary

This is a **trading platform** with web, mobile (Capacitor), and native (React Native) clients. The codebase demonstrates **strong security architecture** with policy-based access control, anti-fraud systems, and audit logging. However, there are several **technical debt items** and **improvement opportunities** identified.

| Category | Status |
|----------|--------|
| Security Architecture | ✅ Strong |
| Type Safety | ⚠️ Needs Improvement |
| Code Organization | ⚠️ Mixed |
| Testing | ⚠️ Limited |
| Documentation | ✅ Good |

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

### 1.1 Project Structure

| Component | Technology | Lines | Status |
|-----------|------------|-------|--------|
| Web Frontend | React + Vite + TanStack Query | ~73 components, 17 pages | Active |
| Backend API | Express + TypeScript | ~4900 lines (routes.ts) | Active |
| Database | PostgreSQL + Drizzle ORM | 177 schema items | Active |
| Mobile (WebView) | Capacitor | Wrapper for web app | Active |
| Native Apps | React Native | 12 screens, 10 components | Active |

