## 4. Database Schema Analysis

### 4.1 Schema Overview

The schema ([schema.pg.ts](file:///\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\home\bcodex\TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY\shared\schema.pg.ts)) is well-structured with **177 items**:

| Category | Tables | Purpose |
|----------|--------|---------|
| User Management | `users`, `userSessions`, `userVerification` | Identity & auth |
| Trading | `trades`, `symbolConfigs` | Core business logic |
| Audit | `identityAudit`, `tradeAudit` | Compliance |
| Grift Detection | `botRiskAssessments`, `signupFingerprints` | Anti-fraud |
| Legal | `legalDocuments`, `legalAcceptances` | Compliance |

### 4.2 Schema Strengths

- ✅ Proper relations defined with Drizzle
- ✅ Zod validation schemas auto-generated
- ✅ Comprehensive audit columns (timestamps, actor tracking)
- ✅ Device fingerprinting for fraud detection

